--verification-cache no longer keys results by the resource limit. Each result keeps the resource use u its solver reported and the limit L it was produced under, and a run with limit L' reuses it only where a fresh run gives the same verdict: valid results with no limit or L' >= u, errors with L' >= u (or L' = L when the solver stopped at its limit), and resource exhaustion at L with 0 < L' <= L. Resource exhaustion reused under a smaller limit reports the count recorded at L. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/261.
